RLS policies have been successfully implemented for Users, Channels, Posts, Comments, and Channel Moderators tables with the following controls:

- Users can read public profiles, update and delete only their own profile.
- Channels are readable by all, can be created by authenticated users, and only owners can update or delete.
- Posts can be read by users with access to the post's channel, inserted by authenticated users, and updated/deleted by authors, channel moderators, or owners.
- Comments can be read on accessible posts, inserted by authenticated users on accessible posts, and updated/deleted by comment authors, post authors, moderators, or owners.
- Channel moderators lists are readable by all, only owners can add moderators, and only owners or moderators themselves can remove moderators.

All policies use the session helper function `app_current_user_id()` and pre-created helper functions for ownership and moderator checks. RLS is enabled on all involved tables.

Task completed.
